{% comment %}
  "How it works" (For Organisations page, "03 How it works" in the client's Figma): a heading and lead
  over four steps in a row. Each step is an auto-numbered eyebrow ("STEP 01"), a title and a line of
  copy. Steps are section-local blocks, so the client can reorder them and the numbers follow.

  Each step leads with a 56px circle in color2 holding a 24px color4 glyph, and a 1px color3 rail runs
  behind the circles from the centre of the first to the centre of the last - the Figma's "Connector
  rail". At 750-989px the steps go two-up and the rail is dropped, since one horizontal line no longer
  describes the sequence. Below 750px they become a vertical timeline: the rail runs down the left
  through the badge centres and the copy sits beside it.

  Salvaged from the earlier wholesale-page branch and brought onto the type ladder: that version drew a
  card with an illustration per step and set the copy at 20px. An intermediate pass replaced the badges
  with a plain hairline above each column, which did not match the mockup - the circles and the rail are
  in the Figma and are restored here.

  Icons. The Figma draws a document-and-pencil, a group of three people, an invoice and a
  stopwatch with a tick. Horizon's built-in set has none of those, so the four were stood in with
  clipboard / map pin / price tag / stopwatch and the client rejected that three times. They now
  come from Tabler Icons (MIT) through snippets/icon-foot-tree.liquid, which carries the licence
  notice and the normalisation that matches them to Horizon's hairline weight. The Figma's icons
  themselves are raster stock of unknown provenance and are deliberately not used. The "Icon
  image" picker still overrides the select, per icon-or-image.liquid.

  Type: .h2 for the heading, .h4 on the step titles (24px), --font-size--2xs for the eyebrow,
  --font-paragraph--size for copy.

  The step title is an <h3> tag on the h4 preset. It was .h3 (28px), which sat too close to the
  32px section heading above it and read as a second section title rather than a step. The Figma
  draws it at 26px, which is not a rung on the ladder, so it snaps down to 24 rather than up.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="section-background"></div>

<div
  class="section section--narrow wholesale-steps spacing-style"
  style="
    {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
    --wholesale-steps-heading: {{ settings.color_palette.foreground }};
    --wholesale-steps-accent: {{ settings.color_palette.color4 }};
    --wholesale-steps-line: {{ settings.color_palette.color3 }};
    --wholesale-steps-soft: {{ settings.color_palette.color8 }};
    --wholesale-steps-badge-bg: {{ settings.color_palette.background }};
    --ws-step-count: {{ section.blocks.size }};
  "
  data-testid="wholesale-steps"
>
  <div class="wholesale-steps__inner">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank or section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
      <div class="wholesale-steps__heading">
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="h2 wholesale-steps__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="wholesale-steps__intro">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <ol class="wholesale-steps__list">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        <li class="wholesale-step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- if block.settings.icon != 'none' or block.settings.image != blank -%}
            <span class="wholesale-step__badge" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- render 'icon-or-image',
                icon: block.settings.icon,
                image_upload: block.settings.image,
                width: 32,
                class_name: 'wholesale-step__icon'
              -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="wholesale-step__body">
            <p class="wholesale-step__eyebrow">
              {{- section.settings.step_label }}
              {% if forloop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ forloop.index -}}
            </p>
            {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
              <h3 class="h4 wholesale-step__title">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
              <p class="wholesale-step__text">{{ block.settings.text }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .wholesale-steps__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  .wholesale-steps__heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  /* .h2 / .h3 paint with `color: var(--color)`, so the colour goes in through --color. */
  .wholesale-steps__title {
    --color: var(--wholesale-steps-heading);

    margin: 0;
  }

  .wholesale-steps__intro {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 640px;
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph--size);
    line-height: var(--line-height--body-loose);
    color: var(--wholesale-steps-soft);
  }

  /* Figma "03 How it works": each step is a circle holding a color4 glyph, and a 1px color3
     "Connector rail" runs behind them from the centre of the first circle to the centre of
     the last. The Figma draws the badge at 72px; it read too heavy against the 12px step
     label next to it, so the badge is 56 and the glyph 24 (48/22 on mobile).

     The badge takes the page background, not color2. The earlier mockup filled it pale green;
     the current one drops that fill, so the glyph reads bare. The circle still has to paint
     something opaque rather than be removed: the rail runs through the badge centre, so a
     transparent badge would let it cross the glyph. Painting it the background colour masks
     the rail and leaves nothing visible. */
  .wholesale-steps__list {
    --ws-badge: 56px;
    --ws-gap: 24px;

    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--ws-step-count, 4), minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--ws-gap);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* The rail stops at the centre of the outer badges rather than running edge to edge.
     A column is (100% - gaps) / count wide, so the right inset is that column width less
     half a badge. Driven by --ws-step-count so it still lands if a step is added. */
  .wholesale-steps__list::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: calc(var(--ws-badge) / 2);
    inset-inline-start: calc(var(--ws-badge) / 2);
    inset-inline-end: calc(
      (100% - (var(--ws-gap) * (var(--ws-step-count, 4) - 1))) / var(--ws-step-count, 4) - var(--ws-badge) / 2
    );
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--wholesale-steps-line);
  }

  .wholesale-step {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .wholesale-step__badge {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex: none;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: var(--ws-badge);
    height: var(--ws-badge);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--wholesale-steps-badge-bg);
  }

  /* `width` needs !important and the glyph needs object-fit, both only because of the uploaded
     image path: icon-or-image writes an inline `style="width: <width>px"` onto the <img>, and an
     inline style outranks every selector, so the image came out 32 wide against this rule's 24
     tall and the square PNG was stretched. The inline SVG path is unaffected by either. */
  .wholesale-step__icon {
    display: block;
    width: 24px !important;
    height: 24px;
    object-fit: contain;
    color: var(--wholesale-steps-accent);
  }

  .wholesale-step__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .wholesale-step__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-subheading--family);
    font-weight: var(--font-subheading--weight);
    font-size: var(--font-size--2xs);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--wholesale-steps-accent);
  }

  .wholesale-step__title {
    --color: var(--wholesale-steps-heading);

    margin: 0;
  }

  .wholesale-step__text {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph--size);
    line-height: var(--line-height--body-loose);
    color: var(--wholesale-steps-soft);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 989px) and (min-width: 750px) {
    .wholesale-steps__list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      row-gap: 40px;
    }

    /* two rows of two, so a single horizontal rail no longer describes the sequence */
    .wholesale-steps__list::before {
      content: none;
    }
  }

  /* Below 750px the steps become a vertical timeline: the rail runs down the left
     through the centre of each badge, and the copy sits beside it. The rail is drawn
     per step rather than once on the list so it starts and stops at badge centres -
     it runs from under one badge to the top of the next, and the last step has none. */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .wholesale-steps__list {
      --ws-badge: 48px;
      --ws-gap: 28px;

      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .wholesale-steps__list::before {
      content: none;
    }

    .wholesale-step {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: var(--ws-badge) minmax(0, 1fr);
      column-gap: 16px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .wholesale-step:not(:last-child)::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset-block-start: var(--ws-badge);
      inset-block-end: calc(-1 * var(--ws-gap));
      inset-inline-start: calc(var(--ws-badge) / 2);
      width: 1px;
      background-color: var(--wholesale-steps-line);
    }

    .wholesale-step__icon {
      width: 22px !important;
      height: 22px;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .wholesale-steps__inner {
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .wholesale-steps__list {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Wholesale steps",
  "class": "section-wholesale-steps",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Leave it to us to handle your corporate needs"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Lead",
      "default": "From the first call to the next reorder — four steps, one point of contact."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "step_label",
      "label": "Step label",
      "info": "Shown before the step number, for example STEP 01.",
      "default": "Step"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 80
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "options": [
            { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
            { "value": "document_pencil", "label": "Document and pencil" },
            { "value": "people_group", "label": "Group of people" },
            { "value": "invoice", "label": "Invoice" },
            { "value": "stopwatch_check", "label": "Stopwatch with tick" },
            { "value": "clipboard", "label": "Clipboard" },
            { "value": "map_pin", "label": "Map pin" },
            { "value": "ruler", "label": "Ruler" },
            { "value": "price_tag", "label": "Price tag" },
            { "value": "box", "label": "Box" },
            { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" },
            { "value": "stopwatch", "label": "Stopwatch" },
            { "value": "return", "label": "Return" },
            { "value": "check_box", "label": "Check box" },
            { "value": "shoe", "label": "Shoe" },
            { "value": "star", "label": "Star" }
          ],
          "default": "document_pencil"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Icon image",
          "info": "Optional. Replaces the icon above."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Tell us what you need"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "Sector, headcount and the sizes you expect. A call or the form below."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Wholesale steps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "document_pencil",
            "title": "Tell us what you need",
            "text": "Sector, headcount and the sizes you expect. A call or the form below."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "people_group",
            "title": "We fit on site",
            "text": "We bring sample sizes to your workplace and fit every pair of feet."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "invoice",
            "title": "One quotation, one delivery",
            "text": "One price list, one invoice, every size in a single delivery."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "stopwatch_check",
            "title": "Reorders in days",
            "text": "Your sizes stay on file, so new starters are fitted without a new survey."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
